                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "778b6094-07ad-3ce0-9846-158216141c0c",
                                        "entry_id": "4e7d4ee9-09fb-3c3f-ba35-1dc61836bcd9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Showily."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b589409-413a-4d78-87ac-d5dc61d1c818",
                                                "sense_id": "778b6094-07ad-3ce0-9846-158216141c0c",
                                                "text": "The highway to the East Coast which ran through the borough of Ebbfield had always been a main road and even now, despite the vast garages, the pylons and the gaily painted factory glasshouses which had sprung up beside it, there still remained an occasional trace of past cultures."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1e9f3b18-f289-4c2b-9f9f-dc4f1b89049f",
                        "source_entry_id": "6c9122d1-a0e0-3a09-819f-dec7590533be",
                        "source_sense_id": "7f870837-128a-3306-90ce-7a57f32734e9",
                        "target_lang_word": "gorgeously",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gorgeously",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f52a1b37-c380-39df-bd69-44f2c4c76c1b",
                                        "entry_id": "d1e18dbe-ec10-3542-b18e-2c95dc9b6a11",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a gorgeous manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8eb11c6-93b3-4e1b-b1af-e6f9cfe703ee",
                                                "sense_id": "f52a1b37-c380-39df-bd69-44f2c4c76c1b",
                                                "text": "Some of these were dressed most gorgeously, others becomingly, and several sneaked in with fantail bangers, calling themselves \"Gentlemen of the Nineteenth Century.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "290ecb9f-fa40-4049-8b98-23517966cd7c",
                                                "sense_id": "f52a1b37-c380-39df-bd69-44f2c4c76c1b",
                                                "text": "What other television show would feature a gorgeously designed sequence where a horrifically mutated Pierre and Marie Curie, their bodies swollen to Godzilla-like proportions from prolonged exposure to the radiation that would eventually kill them, destroy an Asian city with their bare hands like vengeance-crazed monster-Gods?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e488491b-6779-42d2-b157-fa45dc1d5a2e",
                        "source_entry_id": "6c9122d1-a0e0-3a09-819f-dec7590533be",
                        "source_sense_id": "7f870837-128a-3306-90ce-7a57f32734e9",
                        "target_lang_word": "vividly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vividly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e323e116-8f39-3d88-944a-ec253e7348b0",
                                        "entry_id": "7abacc78-af82-38d0-90a9-b3f0e24d83c2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a vivid manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2961c25-eb2a-4c3f-a8e6-af65e808a116",
                                                "sense_id": "e323e116-8f39-3d88-944a-ec253e7348b0",
                                                "text": "Here, in the transept and choir, where the service was being held, one was conscious every moment of an increasing brightness; colours glowing vividly beneath the circular chandeliers, and the rows of small lights on the choristers' desks flashed and sparkled in front of the boys' faces, deep linen collars, and red neckbands."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "084e1a3b-3104-4b6a-81d4-685a6cedda22",
                                                "sense_id": "e323e116-8f39-3d88-944a-ec253e7348b0",
                                                "text": "The water-level route, the whistle and the loud staccato exhaust of this great engine recalled most vividly memories of the New York Central Hudsons highballing along the Hudson River between Harmon and Albany!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b84dbc8f-c541-4402-aa00-73fc0a812d13",
                                                "sense_id": "e323e116-8f39-3d88-944a-ec253e7348b0",
                                                "text": "The Campbell family’s fascination with white supremacy was vividly expressed in the names of Adolf’s two siblings, “Honszlynn Hinler Jeannie Campbell,” an homage to Heinrich Himmler, and “JoyceLynn Aryan Nation Campbell.”² In selecting their children’s peculiar names, the Campbells had exercised a right specifically recognized in New Jersey statutory law, which states, “The designation of a child’s name including the surname is the right of the child’s parent(s).”³"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
